test(update): pin the partial-clone fold and maintenance keys as behavior

Replaces the salvaged tests, which mocked subprocess and the gc command line,
with real-git invariants on a blobless clone:

- lazy-fetch packs fold, keep their .promisor markers, and the history still
  reads under GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH, with the maintenance keys applied (gc.auto=0
  makes this fail);
- the fold adds no pack for commits a Bloom commit-graph has not seen (11
  packs instead of 1 without the guards);
- `hermes update --check`'s debris cleanup is where the fold happens;
- a full clone keeps git's stock maintenance.

i18n(desktop): translate the preview tab pin/unpin labels in de, es, fr, ru

The re-landed pin-to-workspace menu shipped en/ja/zh/zh-hant/ar strings;
the other locales fell back to English.

node: Bridge ChargeFailure manually

This already has to be done for the error it's going to be part of;
might as well be consistent.
